<h1 class=3D"text-3xl font-extrabold tracking-tight">Profiling Rust code wi=
th flamegraphs</h1>
<p class=3D"text-sm text-slate-500">Anika Rao =C2=B7 5 October 2026 =C2=B7 =
6 min read</p>
<p>A flamegraph shows where a program spends its time, one box for every fu=
nction on the stack, as wide as the time it took. Reading one takes a littl=
e practice, but after a few minutes the wide plateaus jump out at you and t=
he narrow spikes stop being distracting.</p>
<img class=3D"rounded-xl shadow" src=3D"https://cdn.ferris-notes.example/im=
g/hero-400.jpg" alt=3D"A flamegraph of the server">
<h2 id=3D"recording" class=3D"group scroll-mt-20">Recording a profile <a hr=
ef=3D"https://ferris-notes.example/posts/flamegraphs#recording" class=3D"op=
acity-0 group-hover:opacity-100">#</a></h2>
<p>To record a profile, build the program in release mode with debug symbol=
s and run it under perf with call graphs turned on.</p>
<div class=3D"relative overflow-hidden md:hidden rounded-lg bg-slate-900"><=
pre class=3D"overflow-x-auto p-4 text-sm"><code class=3D"language-rust">fn =
main() { let map =3D build_map_once(); serve(&amp;map); }</code></pre></div=
>
<ol start=3D"3"><li>Build with <code>--release</code>.</li><li>Run under <c=
ode>perf record -g</code>.</li><li>Fold the stacks and draw the graph.</li>=
</ol>
<h2>Reading the graph</h2>
<p>The first thing to look for is a plateau that should not be there, a fun=
ction that you expected to be cheap taking a quarter of the width. In our c=
ase it was the hash function of a map that was rebuilt for every request in=
stead of once at start-up.</p>
<p><img src=3D"https://cdn.ferris-notes.example/img/chart.png" alt=3D"Time =
per request before and after"></p>
<p>Moving the map into a static that is built lazily cut the time for a req=
uest from eleven milliseconds to four.</p>
<h3>Other views</h3>
<p>Flamegraphs are not the only view worth having, and a flat profile sorte=
d by self time still answers some questions faster.</p>
<dl><dt>Self time</dt><dd>The time spent in the function itself.</dd><dt>To=
tal time</dt><dd>The time spent in it and everything it calls.</dd></dl>
<p><img src=3D"https://cdn.ferris-notes.example/img/anim.gif" alt=3D"The tw=
o profiles side by side"></p>
<p><img src=3D"https://cdn.ferris-notes.example/img/diagram.svg" alt=3D"Whe=
re the time went"></p>
<p><img src=3D"https://cdn.ferris-notes.example/img/wide.jpg" alt=3D"The wh=
ole flamegraph"></p>
<p>The second profile, after the fix, has no plateau at all: the time is sp=
read across parsing, the database and writing the answer.</p>
<img src=3D"https://cdn.ferris-notes.example/img/pixel.gif" width=3D"1" hei=
ght=3D"1" alt=3D"">
</main>
